# An Omen spell that is countered is put into its owner's graveyard like any spell, not shuffled into the library (CR
# 720.3d applies only as it resolves; the ruling: "If an Omen spell is countered ... it won't be shuffled into its owner's
# library"). Bot1 casts Charring Bite at its own Llanowar Elves and Bot2 counters it: Twinmaw Stormbrood is in Bot1's
# graveyard and Bot1's library is unchanged. Nothing lets Bot1 cast a card from its graveyard, so neither face of the
# Twinmaw there is offered (CR 601.3), while the second Twinmaw, in the hand, is cast as Charring Bite on turn 5 (the
# positive control) and kills the Elves, and that one is shuffled into the library.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Twinmaw Stormbrood
Twinmaw Stormbrood
Mountain
Island x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x12

